Package: protectme
Version: 0.1.0
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.31), libbpf1 (>= 0.6), libelf1 (>= 0.176), systemd (>= 245), linux-image-5.2 | linux-image-5.4 | linux-image-5.10 | linux-image-5.15 | linux-image-6.0 | linux-image-6.1 | linux-image-6.2 | linux-image-6.3 | linux-image-6.4 | linux-image-6.5 | linux-image-6.6 | linux-image-6.7 | linux-image-6.8 | linux-image-6.9 | linux-image-6.10 | linux-image-6.11
Recommends: linux-headers-generic
Maintainer: Protectme Team <protectme@dotlinux26.github.io>
Description: Kernel-enforced filesystem safety layer
 Protectme prevents accidental destructive operations (rm -rf, find -delete,
 shutil.rmtree, custom traversal) on protected filesystem trees while allowing
 normal mutation operations. Uses BPF-LSM for kernel enforcement with explicit
 FD-based capability authorization.
 .
 Features:
  * Tool-independent enforcement (rm, find, python, custom C)
  * FD-based capability model (possession = authority)
  * Persistent policy with automatic reconciliation
  * Epoch-based global revoke (O(1))
  * Rename-out and cross-filesystem rename protection
  * OverlayFS lower-layer protection
  * Ancestor boundary walk (PM_WALK_MAX=16)
  * Heartbeat DEAD-state visibility
Homepage: https://github.com/dotlinux26/protectme
